{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall do all His commandments which I command you this day.</b> After it said 'and you shall return' (ושבת), and it said 'and you shall turn' (ואתה תשוב), it added and said: 'which I command you this day.' And so it said above: 'according to all that I command you this day.' This is to explain that the essence of repentance is nothing but to grasp and uphold the way of the Torah of Moses, and therefore it mentions together with repentance each time: 'which I command you this day.' And this is the matter Jeremiah said (Jeremiah 2:17): 'הלא זאת תעשה לך עזבך את ה׳ אלהיך בעת מוליכך בדרך' — that is, on the known way, which is the way of the Torah of Moses, in which your earliest forefathers held fast."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:18.754109871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}